hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"174","Allāhumma ḥawālaynā wa lā `alaynā. Allāhumma `ala ‘l-ākāmi waẓ-ẓirāb, wa buṭūni ‘l-awdiyati, wa manābitish-shajar. O Allah, let the rain fall around us and not upon us, O Allah, (let it fall) on the pastures, hills, valleys, and the roots of trees. Reference: Al-Bukhari 1/224, Muslim 1/614"
"175","Allāhu Akbar, Allāhumma ahillahu ʿalaynā bil-amni wal-īmān, was-salāmi wal-islām, wat-tawfīqi limā tuḥibbu Rabbanā wa tarḍā, Rabbunā wa Rabbuka Allāh.. God is the Greatest. O Allah, bring this new moon to us with security and faith, peace and Islam, and with success in what our Lord loves and is pleased with. Our Lord and your Lord is Allah."
